.TH DNS_RCrewrite 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
dns_resolvconfrewrite \- Resolve domain names using rewrite rules from resolv.conf

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/dns.h>

.IB int
.IB dns_resolvconfrewrite(stralloc* out);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBdns_resolvconfrewrite\fR function resolves domain names using rewrite rules derived from the resolv.conf file. The function reads the DNS rewrite rules from the environment variable DNSREWRITEFILE, the local domain from the environment variable LOCALDOMAIN, or the search domains from the /etc/resolv.conf file. The resolved rules are stored in a static string allocation.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 on success, and -1 on failure.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBdns_resolvconfrewrite\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/dns.h>

int main() {
    stralloc out;

    if (dns_resolvconfrewrite(&out) == 0) {
        printf("DNS Rewrite Rules: %s\n", out.s);
    } else {
        printf("Failed to resolve DNS rewrite rules\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
.nef